titanfall 2's multiplayer is a chaotic  and frenetic affair which often makes it  difficult for beginners to keep up with  that's why we've compiled 11 tips to  help you build up your skills so you can  be well on your way to becoming a master  Titan pilot number one play single  player first titanfall two single-player  campaign is a great place to learn the  basics needed to take on multiplayer  from wall running to the various  strengths and weaknesses of each Titan  type the five-hour campaign offers  plenty of scenarios for you to test the  game systems physics and mechanics  number two learn and understand the wall  run titanfall 2 is all about movement  the faster you are the harder you are to  kill but if you want to go fast you'll  need to master the wall run as it  drastically increases your movement  speed the game's maps are packed with  vertical surfaces so be sure to run  across them to build up momentum combine  it with your double jump to cross gaps  to keep your wall run chain going the  extra jump can also be a handy way to  throw off enemy fire but be aware that  doing so slows you down when chained  methodically wall running can make you  an untouchable foe but if used  senselessly you'll be an easy target  number three picking a Titan each of the  game's six Titans have their own  distinct play styles on loadouts  ion is a well rounded Titan recommended  for beginners and great at mid-range  combat scorch is a Titan focus on area  of effect damage it's at its strongest  when pulling in multiple enemy Titans  with its ignitable gas traps North Star  is a sniper Titan that's best use behind  frontlines it packs a lot of firepower  but is weak in close range combat Ronin  is a hit and run Titan with powerful  melee attacks and great maneuverability  tonne is a Titan that can lock on in  fire missiles at enemy Titans and if you  smartly these missiles can curve around  corners and hit foes hiding in cover  Legion is a Titan that's good at all  ranges but needs time to charge up its  minigun which can be destructive  powerhouse when allowed to fully unload  number 4 spend your credits wisely  double check when an item you want  unlocks since you might be getting it  sooner than you think through level  progression it's better to spend your  hard-earned credits on items boosts and  perks that are unlockable further down  the road number 5 be a team player with  batteries when you're lucky enough to  snag a battery from the enemy  into a friendly tighten this boosts not  only its shields but also greatly  increases your titanfall meter however  if your ticker is at 90% save it for  your own title smart battery use can  turn the tide of battle but be careful  batteries glow when stepped onto your  back which makes you an easy target  number 6 how to fight Titans as a pilot  Titans can be intimidating foes to run  into but if you're smart you can take  one down with ease first throw an arc  grenade or use a fire starter blinded  this allows you to get close then engage  your grapple and use it as a fulcrum to  zip over a Titan and onto its back so  you can pry away its battery or throw  grenades down it but make sure to avoid  grappling the front of an enemy Titan  though if this tactic isn't for you  try using cloak to sneak up on the Titan  to pull their battery that way but be  mindful they can see the sparks of your  jump Jets a Titan isn't defenseless  though if it deploys its electric smoke  attack jump off immediately and stock it  until the smoke clears number 7 don't  rely on anti-titan weapon anti-titan  weapons might seem useful to bring into  battle but most of the time they're not  that effective it's better to focus your  attention on taking out pilots or AI  enemies if you're playing bounty hunt or  attrition so equip that weapon slot with  something that'll help you pick them off  however if you do bring an anti Titan  weapon into battle we recommend the  magnetic grenade launcher it's a handy  weapon useful for both Titan and pilot  combat number eight know when to move  and when to stay still by design  titanfall 2 demands that you keep moving  to survive enemy gunfire but sometimes  it helps to slow things down to mess  with your enemy's expectations try  cloaking yourself and waiting for  enemies to pass by to surprise attack  you can also hunker down and use the a  wall ability a pilot sized particle  shield that enhances outgoing shots  making it essential for sniping  defending the flag or holding down hard  points number 9 mow down AI enemies if  pilots are giving you a hard time and  bounty hunter attrition try bumping up  your team's score by ticking out AI  enemies see a group of grunts toss a  frag or fire started them and keep  moving don't go out of your way for AI  but do your best to kill them whenever  convenient single digits can often  determine matches in bounty hunter  attrition so it helps to kill AI to help  your  team in the long run as well as speed up  your titanfall number 10 understand  boosts titanfall 2 contains items called  boosts which are equippable enhancements  you can use once your titanfall meter  reaches a certain percentage for  instance the map pack boost reveals  enemies to your entire team once your  titanfall reaches 70% there are plenty  of boosts choose from so it's important  to figure out which one works for you  but choose wisely  you can only equip one boost at a time  and they cannot be switched mid match  number 11 check your inbox often for  goodies as you level up a character  known as The Advocate will send messages  to your titanfall to inbox these  messages contain special goodies like  call signs and blooms and camos for both  your Titan and pilot and those are 11  beginners tips to get you started in  titanfall two's multiplayer practice put  them to good use and good luck in the  field  you
 

